Are solutions necessarily homogeneous mixtures?

Yes, according to the ontology, every instance of :Solution is an instance of :HomogeneousMixture, as asserted by the axiom:

:Solution  rdf:type owl:Class;
           owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Class;
                                 owl:intersectionOf ( :HomogeneousMixture ... )
                               ] .

Therefore, all solutions are necessarily homogeneous mixtures in this ontology.

